===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|time}} A [[length]] of [[time]]. {{defdate|from 17th c.}}
#: {{ux|en|There was a '''period''' of confusion following the announcement.}}
#: {{ux|en|You'll be on probation for a six-month '''period'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian|date=December 14, 2011|author=Steven Morris
|title=Devon woman jailed for 168 days for killing kitten in microwave
|url=http://www.guardian.co.uk/world/2011/dec/14/woman-killed-kitten-microwave-jail
|passage=Philip Miles, defending, said: "This was a single instance, there was no allegation of continuing behaviour over a long '''period''' of time."}}
# {{senseid|en|era}} A length of time in history seen as a single coherent entity; an [[epoch]], [[era]]. {{defdate|from 16th c.}}
#: {{syn|en|vintage}}
#: {{ux|en|Food rationing continued in the post-war '''period'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Maxwell Mirror and the Lamp|chapter=7|passage=With some of it on the south and more of it on the north of the great main thoroughfare that connects Aldgate and the East India Docks, St. Bede's at this '''period''' of its history was perhaps the poorest and most miserable parish in the East End of London.}}
