# {{senseid|en|menstruation}} {{lb|en|euphemism}} Female [[menstruation]]; an episode of this. {{defdate|from 18th c.}}
#: {{ux|en|When she is on her '''period''', she prefers not to go swimming.}}
## {{senseid|en|symptoms}} The set of [[symptom]]s [[associate]]d with menstruation, even if not accompanied by menstruation; an episode of these symptoms.<!--covers e.g. periods in trans women-->
# {{senseid|en|art}} A section of an artist's, writer's (etc.) career distinguished by a given quality, preoccupation etc. {{defdate|from 19th c.}}
#: {{ux|en|This is one of the last paintings Picasso created during his Blue '''Period'''.}}
# {{senseid|en|school}} Each of the divisions into which a [[school]] day is split, allocated to a given subject or activity. {{defdate|from 19th c.}}
#: {{ux|en|I have math class in second '''period'''.}}
# {{senseid|en|sports}} {{lb|en|sports|primarily|ice hockey}} Each of the intervals, typically three, of which a game is divided. {{defdate|from 19th c.}}
#: {{ux|en|Gretzky scored in the last minute of the second '''period'''.}}
# {{senseid|en|overtime}} {{lb|en|sports|primarily|ice hockey}} One or more additional intervals to decide a tied game, an [[overtime]] period.
#: {{ux|en|They won in the first overtime '''period'''.}}
